{
  "nbformat": 4,
  "nbformat_minor": 5,
  "metadata": {
    "kernelspec": {
      "name": "maxima",
      "display_name": "Maxima",
      "language": "maxima"
    },
    "aximar": {}
  },
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# Orbits Around a Black Hole\n\nOutside a non-rotating black hole of mass $M$, spacetime follows the Schwarzschild metric. This notebook builds that metric with Maxima's `ctensor` package and derives the geodesic equations from it. They reduce to a single orbit equation for $u = 1/r$ that differs from Newton's by one term, $3Mu^2$. The effective potential then gives the innermost stable circular orbit at $r = 6M$ and the photon sphere at $r = 3M$.\n\nThe numeric half integrates bound orbits with CVODE and measures how far the perihelion advances on each turn. The measured shift matches an exact elliptic-integral formula to many digits. It approaches the weak-field result $6\\pi M/(a(1 - e^2))$ far from the hole and exceeds it close in. A last section bends light past the hole and compares the deflection with $4M/b$. Units are geometric throughout, $G = c = 1$, so lengths are in units of $M$.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "load(\"ctensor\")$\nload(\"numerics\")$\nload(\"numerics-sundials\")$\nload(\"ax-plots\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 1,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## The Schwarzschild Metric [S]\n\nIn coordinates $(t, r, \\theta, \\varphi)$ the line element is\n\n$$ds^2 = -\\left(1 - \\frac{2M}{r}\\right)dt^2 + \\frac{dr^2}{1 - 2M/r} + r^2\\,d\\theta^2 + r^2\\sin^2\\theta\\,d\\varphi^2$$\n\n`ctensor` takes the metric as the matrix `lg`. `christof` then computes the Christoffel symbols of the second kind into `mcs[i,j,k]` $= \\Gamma^k_{ij}$. Of the nonzero ones, five enter equatorial orbits ($\\theta = \\pi/2$). The sixth, $\\Gamma^\\theta_{\\varphi\\varphi} = -\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta$, vanishes on the equator, so an orbit that starts in the equatorial plane stays there.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "ct_coords : [t, r, theta, phi]$\nlg : matrix([-(1 - 2*M/r), 0, 0, 0],\n            [0, 1/(1 - 2*M/r), 0, 0],\n            [0, 0, r^2, 0],\n            [0, 0, 0, r^2*sin(theta)^2])$\ncmetric(false)$\nchristof(false)$\nequatorial : [theta = %pi/2]$\n/* label atoms that print as Gamma^k_ij */\ngammas : [[G_t_tr, \"\\\\Gamma^{t}_{tr}\", mcs[1,2,1]],\n          [G_r_tt, \"\\\\Gamma^{r}_{tt}\", factor(mcs[1,1,2])],\n          [G_r_rr, \"\\\\Gamma^{r}_{rr}\", mcs[2,2,2]],\n          [G_r_pp, \"\\\\Gamma^{r}_{\\\\varphi\\\\varphi}\", subst(equatorial, mcs[4,4,2])],\n          [G_p_rp, \"\\\\Gamma^{\\\\varphi}_{r\\\\varphi}\", mcs[2,4,4]],\n          [G_th_pp, \"\\\\Gamma^{\\\\theta}_{\\\\varphi\\\\varphi}\", subst(equatorial, mcs[4,4,3])]]$\nfor g in gammas do texput(g[1], g[2])$\nmap(lambda([g], g[1] = g[3]), gammas);",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 2,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "text/latex": [
              "\\left[ \\Gamma^{t}_{tr}={{M}\\over{r^2-2\\,M\\,r}} , \\Gamma^{r}_{tt}={{M\\,\\left( r-2\\,M\\right)}\\over{r^3}} , \\Gamma^{r}_{rr}=-\\left({{M}\\over{r^2-2\\,M\\,r}} \\right) , \\Gamma^{r}_{\\varphi\\varphi}=2\\,M-r , \\Gamma^{\\varphi}_{r\\varphi}={{ 1}\\over{r}} , \\Gamma^{\\theta}_{\\varphi\\varphi}=0 \\right] "
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 2,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Geodesic Equations [S]\n\n`cgeodesic` builds $\\ddot x^k + \\Gamma^k_{ij}\\dot x^i \\dot x^j = 0$ for each coordinate, with derivatives taken along the proper time $s$. Setting $\\theta = \\pi/2$ and $\\dot\\theta = \\ddot\\theta = 0$ leaves one equation for each of the other coordinates, and the $\\theta$ equation reduces to $0 = 0$. The helper `tidy` divides each equation by the coefficient of its second derivative and factors each term.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "cgeodesic(false)$\nequator(g) := subst(equatorial, subst(['diff(theta, s, 2) = 0, 'diff(theta, s) = 0], g))$\ndsyms : ['diff(t, s, 2) = tdd, 'diff(r, s, 2) = rdd, 'diff(phi, s, 2) = phidd,\n         'diff(t, s) = td, 'diff(r, s) = rd, 'diff(phi, s) = phid]$\nmonos : [[tdd], [rdd], [phidd], [td, td], [rd, rd], [phid, phid], [td, rd], [rd, phid]]$\nmcoef(n, m) := if length(m) = 1 then coeff(n, m[1], 1)\n  else if m[1] = m[2] then coeff(n, m[1], 2)\n  else coeff(coeff(n, m[1], 1), m[2], 1)$\ntidy(g, x) := block([n : expand(subst(dsyms, num(ratsimp(g))))],\n  subst(map(lambda([e], rhs(e) = lhs(e)), dsyms),\n        lsum(factor(mcoef(n, m)/coeff(n, x, 1))*apply(\"*\", m), m, monos)))$\ngeq : [tidy(equator(geod[1]), tdd), tidy(equator(geod[2]), rdd),\n       equator(geod[3]), tidy(equator(geod[4]), phidd)]$\nmap(lambda([e], e = 0), geq);",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 3,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "text/latex": [
              "\\left[ {{d^2}\\over{d\\,s^2}}\\,t+{{2\\,M\\,\\left({{d}\\over{d\\,s}}\\,r\\right)\\, \\left({{d}\\over{d\\,s}}\\,t\\right)}\\over{r\\,\\left(r-2\\,M\\right)}}=0 , {{M\\, \\left(r-2\\,M\\right)\\,\\left({{d}\\over{d\\,s}}\\,t\\right)^2}\\over{r^3}}+{{d^2 }\\over{d\\,s^2}}\\,r-{{M\\,\\left({{d}\\over{d\\,s}}\\,r\\right)^2}\\over{r\\,\\left(r-2 \\,M\\right)}}-\\left({{d}\\over{d\\,s}}\\,\\varphi\\right)^2\\,\\left(r-2\\,M\\right)=0 , 0=0 , {{2\\,\\left({{d}\\over{d\\,s}}\\,\\varphi\\right)\\,\\left({{d}\\over{d\\,s}} \\,r\\right)}\\over{r}}+{{d^2}\\over{d\\,s^2}}\\,\\varphi=0 \\right] "
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 3,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Conserved Energy and Angular Momentum [S]\n\nThe metric does not depend on $t$ or $\\varphi$, so the $t$ and $\\varphi$ equations are total derivatives. The conserved quantities are the energy per unit mass $E = (1 - 2M/r)\\,\\dot t$ and the angular momentum per unit mass $L = r^2\\dot\\varphi$. The cell checks that $dE/ds$ and $dL/ds$ are multiples of the geodesic equations, so both vanish along any geodesic.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "Ecap : (1 - 2*M/r)*'diff(t, s)$\nLcap : r^2*'diff(phi, s)$\n[ratsimp(diff(Ecap, s) - (1 - 2*M/r)*geq[1]), ratsimp(diff(Lcap, s) - r^2*geq[4])];",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 4,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "text/latex": [
              "\\left[ 0 , 0 \\right] "
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 4,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "A massive particle's four-velocity has unit length, $g_{\\mu\\nu}\\dot x^\\mu \\dot x^\\nu = -1$. Writing $\\dot t$ and $\\dot\\varphi$ in terms of $E$ and $L$ turns that condition into the radial equation, a first integral of the $r$ geodesic equation.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "norm : -(1 - 2*M/r)*tdot^2 + rdot^2/(1 - 2*M/r) + r^2*phidot^2 = -1$\nradial0 : solve(subst([tdot = E/(1 - 2*M/r), phidot = L/r^2], norm), rdot^2)[1]$\nradial : rdot^2 = expand(E^2 - (1 - 2*M/r)*(1 + L^2/r^2))$\nprint(\"solve result equals E^2 - (1 - 2M/r)(1 + L^2/r^2):\", is(ratsimp(rhs(radial) - rhs(radial0)) = 0))$\nradial;",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 5,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "solve result equals E^2 - (1 - 2M/r)(1 + L^2/r^2): true"
          ]
        },
        {
          "data": {
            "text/latex": [
              "{\\it rdot}^2={{2\\,M}\\over{r}}-{{L^2}\\over{r^2}}+{{2\\,L^2\\,M}\\over{r^3}}+E^2- 1"
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 5,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## The Orbit Equation [S]\n\nThe shape of the orbit needs $r$ as a function of $\\varphi$. With $u = 1/r$ and $u' = du/d\\varphi$, the chain rule gives $\\dot r = (dr/d\\varphi)\\,\\dot\\varphi = -L u'$. The radial equation becomes $L^2 u'^2 = F(u)$, a cubic in $u$. Differentiating with respect to $\\varphi$ and dividing by $2L^2 u'$ gives $u'' = F'(u)/(2L^2)$.\n\nThe same steps on Newton's energy equation $\\tfrac12\\dot r^2 - M/r + L^2/(2r^2) = \\epsilon$ give the Newtonian orbit equation for comparison.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "ueq : expand(subst([r = 1/u, rdot = -L*up], radial))$\nF : rhs(ueq)$\norbit_gr : upp + u = expand(diff(F, u)/(2*L^2) + u)$\nnewton : (1/2)*rdot^2 - M/r + L^2/(2*r^2) = eps$\nFn : L^2*rhs(solve(subst([r = 1/u, rdot = -L*up], newton), up^2)[1])$\norbit_n : upp + u = expand(diff(Fn, u)/(2*L^2) + u)$\ntranspose(matrix([ueq, orbit_gr, orbit_n]));",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 6,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "text/latex": [
              "\\ifx\\endpmatrix\\undefined\\pmatrix{\\else\\begin{pmatrix}\\fi L^2\\,{\\it up}^2=2 \\,L^2\\,M\\,u^3-L^2\\,u^2+2\\,M\\,u+E^2-1\\cr {\\it upp}+u=3\\,M\\,u^2+{{M}\\over{L^2}} \\cr {\\it upp}+u={{M}\\over{L^2}}\\cr \\ifx\\endpmatrix\\undefined}\\else\\end{pmatrix}\\fi "
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 6,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "The two equations differ by $3Mu^2$. Relative to the Newtonian term $M/L^2$ it has size $3u^2L^2 \\approx 3(v/c)^2$ for a near-circular orbit, which is about $10^{-7}$ for Mercury and of order one near the hole.\n\n## The Effective Potential [S+N]\n\nDividing the radial equation by two puts it in the form $\\tfrac12\\dot r^2 + V(r) = \\tfrac12(E^2 - 1)$, with\n\n$$V_{\\text{GR}}(r) = -\\frac{M}{r} + \\frac{L^2}{2r^2} - \\frac{ML^2}{r^3}, \\qquad V_{\\text{N}}(r) = -\\frac{M}{r} + \\frac{L^2}{2r^2}$$\n\nThe extra $-ML^2/r^3$ term overwhelms the centrifugal barrier at small $r$. The Newtonian potential rises to infinity as $r \\to 0$, while the relativistic one has a finite peak and then falls into the hole. The plot uses $M = 1$; dashed curves are Newtonian.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "Veff : expand(((1 - 2*M/r)*(1 + L^2/r^2) - 1)/2)$\nVn : -M/r + L^2/(2*r^2)$\n[Veff, Vn];",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 7,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "text/latex": [
              "\\left[ -\\left({{M}\\over{r}}\\right)+{{L^2}\\over{2\\,r^2}}-{{L^2\\,M}\\over{r^3}} , {{L^2}\\over{2\\,r^2}}-{{M}\\over{r}} \\right] "
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 7,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "Ls : [3.6, 4.0, 4.4]$\ncols : [\"steelblue\", \"darkorange\", \"seagreen\"]$\napply(ax_draw2d, append(\n  apply(append, makelist(\n    [color = cols[k], dash = \"solid\", line_width = 2,\n     name = sconcat(\"GR, L = \", Ls[k]),\n     explicit(subst([M = 1, L = Ls[k]], Veff), r, 2.5, 40),\n     dash = \"dash\", name = sconcat(\"Newton, L = \", Ls[k]),\n     explicit(subst([M = 1, L = Ls[k]], Vn), r, 2.5, 40)], k, 1, 3)),\n  [yrange = [-0.1, 0.08], title = \"Effective Potential, GR (solid) and Newton (dashed)\",\n   xlabel = \"r / M\", ylabel = \"V(r)\", grid = true, showlegend = true]))$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 8,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "application/x-maxima-plotly": [
              "{\"data\":[{\"x\":[2.5,2.5751503006012024,2.650300601202405,2.7254509018036073,2.8006012024048097,2.875751503006012,2.9509018036072145,3.026052104208417,3.1012024048096194,3.176352705410822,3.2515030060120242,3.3266533066132267,3.401803607214429,3.4769539078156315,3.552104208416834,3.6272545090180364,3.702404809619239,3.777555110220441,3.8527054108216436,3.927855711422846,4.0030060120240485,4.078156312625251,4.153306613226453,4.228456913827656,4.303607214428858,4.37875751503006,4.453907815631263,4.529058116232465,4.604208416833668,4.679358717434869,4.754509018036073,4.829659318637274,4.904809619238478,4.979959919839679,5.055110220440882,5.130260521042084,5.205410821643287,5.280561122244489,5.355711422845692,5.430861723446894,5.506012024048097,5.5811623246492985,5.656312625250502,5.731462925851703,5.806613226452907,5.881763527054108,5.9569138276553115,6.032064128256513,6.1072144288577155,6.182364729458918,6.25751503006012,6.332665330661323,6.407815631262525,6.482965931863728,6.55811623246493,6.6332665330661325,6.708416833667335,6.783567134268537,6.85871743486974,6.933867735470942,7.009018036072145,7.084168336673347,7.159318637274549,7.234468937875752,7.309619238476954,7.384769539078157,7.459919839679359,7.5350701402805615,7.610220440881764,7.685370741482966,7.760521042084169,7.835671342685371,7.910821643286574,7.985971943887776,8.061122244488978,8.136272545090181,8.211422845691384,8.286573146292586,8.361723446893787,8.43687374749499,8.512024048096194,8.587174348697395,8.662324649298597,8.7374749498998,8.812625250501004,8.887775551102205,8.962925851703407,9.03807615230461,9.113226452905813,9.188376753507015,9.263527054108216,9.33867735470942,9.413827655310623,9.488977955911825,9.564128256513026,9.63927855711423,9.714428857715431,9.789579158316634,9.864729458917836,9.939879759519037,10.01503006012024,10.090180360721444,10.165330661322646,10.240480961923847,10.31563126252505,10.390781563126254,10.465931863727455,10.541082164328659,10.61623246492986,10.691