        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "Circular orbits sit where $V'(r) = 0$. For $L^2 > 12M^2$ there are two: a stable one at the minimum and an unstable one at the peak. They merge when $V' = V'' = 0$ together, which fixes the innermost stable circular orbit (ISCO). The energy there gives the binding energy $1 - E$, the fraction of rest mass that matter radiates as it spirals down to the ISCO through an accretion disc.\n\nA photon has no rest mass, so the $1$ in $(1 + L^2/r^2)$ drops out and its potential is proportional to $(1 - 2M/r)/r^2$. Its single maximum is the photon sphere, where light can circle the hole on an unstable orbit.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "circ_sol : solve(diff(Veff, r) = 0, r)$\nisco_sol : solve([diff(Veff, r) = 0, diff(Veff, r, 2) = 0], [r, L])$\nEisco : radcan(sqrt(subst([r = 6*M, L = 2*sqrt(3)*M], (1 - 2*M/r)*(1 + L^2/r^2))))$\nphoton_sphere : solve(diff((1 - 2*M/r)/r^2, r) = 0, r)$\nprintf(true, \"ISCO binding energy 1 - E = ~,4f (~,2f% of rest mass)~%\", float(1 - Eisco), float(100*(1 - Eisco)))$\n['r[circ] = map(rhs, circ_sol), isco_sol[2], 'E[isco] = Eisco, 'r[photon] = rhs(photon_sphere[1])];",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 9,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "ISCO binding energy 1 - E = 0.0572 (5.72% of rest mass)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "data": {
            "text/latex": [
              "\\left[ r_{{\\it circ}}=\\left[ -\\left({{L\\,\\sqrt{L^2-12\\,M^2}-L^2}\\over{2\\,M}} \\right) , {{L\\,\\sqrt{L^2-12\\,M^2}+L^2}\\over{2\\,M}} \\right]  , \\left[ r=6\\,M , L=2\\,\\sqrt{3}\\,M \\right]  , E_{{\\it isco}}={{2^{{{3}\\over{2}}}}\\over{3}} , r_{{\\it photon}}=3\\,M \\right] "
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 9,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## A Precessing Orbit [S+N]\n\nA bound orbit oscillates between perihelion $r_p$ and aphelion $r_a$, where $u' = 0$. These are two roots $u_1 = 1/r_a$ and $u_2 = 1/r_p$ of the cubic $F(u)/L^2 = 2M(u - u_1)(u - u_2)(u - u_3)$. Matching coefficients gives the third root and $L^2$, so choosing $r_p$ and $r_a$ fixes the orbit.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "cubic : expand(F/L^2)$\nroots3 : expand(2*M*(u - u1)*(u - u2)*(u - u3))$\npeq : makelist(coeff(cubic, u, k) = coeff(roots3, u, k), k, 0, 2)$\nu3sol : solve(peq[3], u3)[1]$\nL2sol : L^2 = 1/rhs(solve(subst(L = 1/sqrt(iL2), peq[2]), iL2)[1])$\n[u3sol, L2sol];",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 10,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "text/latex": [
              "\\left[ u_{3}=-\\left({{2\\,M\\,u_{2}+2\\,M\\,u_{1}-1}\\over{2\\,M}}\\right) , L^2={{ 1}\\over{\\left(u_{2}+u_{1}\\right)\\,u_{3}+u_{1}\\,u_{2}}} \\right] "
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 10,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "The orbit below has $r_p = 15M$ and $r_a = 45M$. CVODE integrates $u'' = M/L^2 + 3Mu^2 - u$ in $\\varphi$ over four turns, starting at perihelion with $u' = 0$. An event on $u'$ falling through zero records each perihelion. The Newtonian ellipse with the same $r_p$ and $r_a$, $u = (1 + e\\cos\\varphi)/p$ with $p = a(1 - e^2)$, closes on itself. The relativistic orbit traces a rosette.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "orbit_params(rp, ra) := block([q : [M = 1, u1 = 1.0/ra, u2 = 1.0/rp]],\n  q : endcons(u3 = subst(q, rhs(u3sol)), q),\n  [rhs(q[2]), rhs(q[3]), rhs(q[4]), subst(q, rhs(L2sol))])$\norbit_rhs(L2v) := subst([M = 1, L = sqrt(L2v), upp = w], [w, rhs(orbit_gr) - u])$\n\n[rp0, ra0] : [15, 45]$\nq0 : orbit_params(rp0, ra0)$\nres0 : np_cvode(orbit_rhs(q0[4]), [ph, u, w], [q0[2], 0.0],\n                np_linspace(0.0, float(8*%pi), 2001), 1e-11, 1e-13, adams, [w], 100000, [-1])$\ntraj0 : first(res0)$\nperi0 : map(first, second(res0))$\nprintf(true, \"L^2 = ~,4f M^2, perihelia at phi = ~{~,4f ~}~%\", q0[4], peri0)$\n\nphs : np_col(traj0, 0)$\nrs : np_div(1.0, np_col(traj0, 1))$\nxs : np_to_list(np_mul(rs, np_cos(phs)))$\nys : np_to_list(np_mul(rs, np_sin(phs)))$\npN : 2.0*rp0*ra0/(rp0 + ra0)$\neN : (ra0 - rp0)/(ra0 + rp0)$\nax_draw2d(\n  color = \"gray\", dash = \"dash\", line_width = 2, name = \"Newtonian ellipse\",\n  parametric(pN*cos(v)/(1 + eN*cos(v)), pN*sin(v)/(1 + eN*cos(v)), v, 0, 2*%pi),\n  color = \"steelblue\", dash = \"solid\", line_width = 1.5, name = \"Schwarzschild orbit\",\n  lines(xs, ys),\n  color = \"crimson\", marker_size = 9, name = \"Perihelia\",\n  points(map(lambda([p], rp0*cos(p)), cons(0.0, peri0)), map(lambda([p], rp0*sin(p)), cons(0.0, peri0))),\n  color = \"black\", line_width = 2, name = \"Horizon r = 2M\",\n  parametric(2*cos(v), 2*sin(v), v, 0, 2*%pi),\n  aspect_ratio = true, title = \"Bound Orbit, r_p = 15M, r_a = 45M, Four Turns\",\n  xlabel = \"x / M\", ylabel = \"y / M\", showlegend = true)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 11,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "L^2 = 26.2987 M^2, perihelia at phi = 7.3422 14.6845 22.0267"
          ]
        },
        {
