8679459350379,-1.177606928318805,-1.157159206858597,-1.1365280234410753,-1.1157166490399075,-1.0947283831971588,-1.0735665535001744,-1.0522345150540044,-1.0307356499494622,-1.00907336672692,-0.9872510998358972,-0.96527230909054,-0.9431404791210938,-0.9208591188214283,-0.8984317607927138,-0.8758619607833545,-0.8531532971252369,-0.830309370166398,-0.8073338017002191,-0.7842302343911945,-0.7610023311974171,-0.7376537747898285,-0.7141882669683453,-0.6906095280749656,-0.6669212964039231,-0.6431273276089929,-0.6192313941080616,-0.5952372844850228,-0.5711488028891117,-0.5469697684317849,-0.5227040145812146,-0.498355388554505,-0.4739277507077474,-0.4494249739239654,-0.42485094299910037,-0.4002095540260908,-0.3755047137771605,-0.35074033908442925,-0.3259203562189131,-0.3010487002680276,-0.27612931451171,-0.25116614979722546,-0.22616316391277466,-0.20112432096001603,-0.1760535907255717,-0.15095494805163162,-0.12583237220577423,-0.10068984625005872,-0.07553135640954242,-0.050360891440278804,-0.025182441996914388,-4.898587196589413e-16],\"type\":\"scatter\",\"mode\":\"lines\",\"line\":{\"color\":\"black\",\"width\":2},\"name\":\"Horizon r = 2M\"}],\"layout\":{\"title\":{\"text\":\"Bound Orbit, r_p = 15M, r_a = 45M, Four Turns\"},\"showlegend\":true,\"width\":700,\"height\":700,\"plot_bgcolor\":\"white\",\"paper_bgcolor\":\"white\",\"xaxis\":{\"title\":{\"text\":\"x / M\"},\"gridcolor\":\"#ddd\",\"linecolor\":\"#ddd\",\"linewidth\":1,\"zerolinecolor\":\"black\",\"zerolinewidth\":1},\"yaxis\":{\"scaleanchor\":\"x\",\"scaleratio\":1.0,\"title\":{\"text\":\"y / M\"},\"gridcolor\":\"#ddd\",\"linecolor\":\"#ddd\",\"linewidth\":1,\"zerolinecolor\":\"black\",\"zerolinewidth\":1}}}"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "display_data"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "The first integral $u'^2 = F(u)/L^2$ holds along an exact solution. CVODE never sees it, so its drift over the four turns measures the integration error.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "uu : np_to_list(np_col(traj0, 1))$\nww : np_to_list(np_col(traj0, 2))$\n/* E^2 from the constant term: (E^2 - 1)/L^2 = -2 M u1 u2 u3 */\nF0 : subst([M = 1, L = sqrt(q0[4]), E = sqrt(1 - 2*q0[1]*q0[2]*q0[3]*q0[4])], F/L^2)$\nfi : map(lambda([uv, wv], wv^2 - subst(u = uv, F0)), uu, ww)$\nprintf(true, \"max |u'^2 - F(u)/L^2| over ~d points: ~,2e~%\", length(fi), lmax(abs(fi)))$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 12,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "max |u'^2 - F(u)/L^2| over 2001 points: 1.84e-13"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Perihelion Shift: Exact and Weak-Field [S]\n\nBetween two perihelia $\\varphi$ advances by $2\\int_{u_1}^{u_2} du / \\sqrt{2M(u - u_1)(u_2 - u)(u_3 - u)}$. The substitution $u = u_1 + (u_2 - u_1)\\sin^2\\chi$ turns this into a complete elliptic integral of the first kind:\n\n$$\\Delta\\varphi_{\\text{orbit}} = \\frac{4K(m)}{\\sqrt{2M(u_3 - u_1)}}, \\qquad m = \\frac{u_2 - u_1}{u_3 - u_1}$$\n\nExpanding $K(m) = \\int_0^{\\pi/2}(1 - m\\sin^2 x)^{-1/2}dx$ in powers of $m$, inserting $u_3 = 1/(2M) - u_1 - u_2$ and expanding in $M$ gives the shift beyond $2\\pi$. With $u_1 + u_2 = 2/p$ the first-order term is $6\\pi M/p$, the weak-field formula. The second-order term is the next correction.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "texput(Dphi, \"\\\\Delta\\\\varphi\")$\nKser : integrate(taylor(1/sqrt(1 - m*sin(x)^2), m, 0, 2), x, 0, %pi/2)$\nper : 4*subst(m = (u2 - u1)/(u3 - u1), Kser)/sqrt(2*M*(u3 - u1))$\nper : subst(u3sol, per)$\nshift_series : factor(subst([u1 = (1 - e)/p, u2 = (1 + e)/p], taylor(per - 2*%pi, M, 0, 2)))$\n['K(m) = Kser, Dphi = shift_series];",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 13,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "text/latex": [
              "\\left[ K\\left(m\\right)={{9\\,\\pi\\,m^2+16\\,\\pi\\,m+64\\,\\pi}\\over{128}} , \\Delta\\varphi={{3\\,\\pi\\,M\\,\\left(4\\,p+M\\,e^2+18\\,M\\right)}\\over{2\\,p^2}} \\right] "
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 13,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "For Mercury, $M_\\odot = 1476.6$ m in geometric units, $a = 5.791\\times10^{10}$ m and $e = 0.2056$. The weak-field formula with 415.2 orbits per century gives the 43 arcseconds per century of Mercury's precession that Newtonian perturbations from the other planets leave unexplained.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "mercury : [M = 1476.6, p = 5.791e10*(1 - 0.2056^2)]$\ndphi_merc : subst(mercury, 6*%pi*M/p)$\nprintf(true, \"Mercury: ~,3e rad per orbit, ~,2f arcsec per century~%\",\n       float(dphi_merc), float(dphi_merc*415.2*180*3600/%pi))$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 14,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Mercury: 5.018e-7 rad per orbit, 42.98 arcsec per century"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Perihelion Shift: Numeric Measurement [N]\n\n`shift_numeric` integrates three and a half turns and averages the gaps between successive perihelia, less $2\\pi$. `shift_exact` evaluates the elliptic-integral formula with `elliptic_kc`. The orbits have $e = 0.5$ ($r_a = 3r_p$) and shrink from $r_p = 1000M$ to $r_p = 8M$. The numeric and exact shifts agree to better than $10^{-8}$ rad in every case. The weak-field ratio starts near one and grows as the orbit approaches the hole, where higher powers of $M/p$ matter.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "shift_numeric(rp, ra, norb) := block([q : orbit_params(rp, ra), res, ph],\n  res : np_cvode(orbit_rhs(q[4]), [ph, u, w], [q[2], 0.0],\n                 [0.0, float(2*%pi*(norb + 0.5))], 1e-11, 1e-13, adams, [w], 100000, [-1]),\n  ph : cons(0.0, map(first, second(res))),\n  (last(ph) - first(ph))/(length(ph) - 1) - float(2*%pi))$\nshift_exact(rp, ra) := block([q : orbit_params(rp, ra)],\n  float(4*elliptic_kc((q[2] - q[1])/(q[3] - q[1]))/sqrt(2*(q[3] - q[1])) - 2*%pi))$\nshift_weak(rp, ra) := float(6*%pi/(2*rp*ra/(rp + ra)))$\n\nprintf(true, \"~6a ~12a ~12a ~10a ~12a ~10a~%\", \"r_p/M\", \"numeric\", \"exact\", \"|num-ex|\", \"weak-field\", \"num/weak\")$\nfor rp in [1000, 300, 100, 30, 15, 8] do block([dn, de, dw],\n  dn : shift_numeric(rp, 3*rp, 3), de : shift_exact(rp, 3*rp), dw : shift_weak(rp, 3*rp),\n  printf(true, \"~6d ~12,5e ~12,5e ~10,1e ~12,5e ~10,4f~%\", rp, dn, de, abs(dn - de), dw, dn/dw))$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 15,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "r_p/M  numeric      exact        |num-ex|   weak-field   num/weak\n  1000   1.26047e-2   1.26047e-2     6.3e-9   1.25664e-2     1.0031\n   300   4.23175e-2   4.23175e-2    1.6e-10   4.18879e-2     1.0103\n   100   1.29622e-1   1.29622e-1    2.1e-10   1.25664e-1     1.0315\n    30   4.66871e-1   4.66871e-1    3.2e-10   4.18879e-1     1.1146\n    15   1.05906e+0   1.05906e+0    1.6e-11   8.37758e-1     1.2642\n     8   2.64958e+0   2.64958e+0    1.8e-10   1.57080e+0     1.6868"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "The same ratio as a curve, from the exact formula over a range of perihelion distances, with the two-term series $\\frac{6\\pi M}{p} + \\frac{3\\pi(18 + e^2)M^2}{2p^2}$ for comparison. The second-order term closes most of the gap down to about $r_p = 20M$.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "rps : makelist(float(8*10^(k/20)), k, 0, 50)$\nratio_exact : map(lambda([rp], shift_exact(rp, 3*rp)/shift_weak(rp, 3*rp)), rps)$\nratio_2nd : map(lambda([rp], float(subst([M = 1, e = 0.5, p = 1.5*rp], shift_series))/shift_weak(rp, 3*rp)), rps)$\nax_draw2d(\n  color = \"steelblue\", line_width = 2, name = \"Exact / weak-field\",\n  lines(rps, ratio_exact),\n  color = \"darkorange\", dash = \"dash\", name = \"Second order / weak-field\",\n  lines(rps, ratio_2nd),\n  logx = true, title = \"Perihelion Shift Relative to 6πM/p (e = 0.5)\",\n  xlabel = \"r_p / M\", ylabel = \"ratio\", grid = true, showlegend = true)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 16,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
