    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Light Bending [S+N]\n\nA photon follows the same orbit equation with $M/L^2 \\to 0$, since $L \\to \\infty$ while the impact parameter $b = L/E$ stays finite. Taking the limit of the relativistic equation:",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "orbit_photon : upp + u = limit(rhs(orbit_gr), L, inf);",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 17,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "text/latex": [
              "{\\it upp}+u=3\\,M\\,u^2"
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 17,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "A photon arriving from $x = +\\infty$ at height $b$ starts at $u = 0$ with $u' = 1/b$ and leaves when $u$ returns to zero. The deflection is the excess of the swept angle over $\\pi$. An independent check evaluates the integral $2\\int_0^{u_0} du/\\sqrt{1/b^2 - u^2 + 2Mu^3} - \\pi$ with `quad_qags`, where $u_0$ is the turning point. The weak-field value is $4M/b$, and the series continues with $15\\pi M^2/(4b^2)$.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "photon_rhs : subst([M = 1, upp = w], [w, rhs(orbit_photon) - u])$\ndeflect_numeric(bv) := block([res],\n  res : np_cvode(photon_rhs, [ph, u, w], [0.0, 1.0/bv], [0.0, 20.0],\n                 1e-11, 1e-13, adams, [u], 100000, [-1]),\n  first(first(second(res))) - float(%pi))$\ndeflect_exact(bv) := block([u0],\n  u0 : second(sort(map(rhs, allroots(float(2*u^3 - u^2 + 1/bv^2))))),\n  2*first(quad_qags(1/sqrt(1/bv^2 - u^2 + 2*u^3), u, 0, u0)) - float(%pi))$\n\nprintf(true, \"~6a ~12a ~12a ~10a ~10a ~10a~%\", \"b/M\", \"numeric\", \"quadrature\", \"4M/b\", \"2nd order\", \"num/(4M/b)\")$\nfor bv in [6, 10, 30, 100, 1000] do block([dn : deflect_numeric(bv), de : deflect_exact(bv)],\n  printf(true, \"~6d ~12,6e ~12,6e ~10,4e ~10,4e ~10,4f~%\",\n         bv, dn, de, 4.0/bv, float(4/bv + 15*%pi/(4*bv^2)), dn/(4.0/bv)))$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 18,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "b/M    numeric      quadrature   4M/b       2nd order  num/(4M/b)\n     6  1.719388e+0  1.719388e+0  6.6667e-1  9.9392e-1     2.5791\n    10  5.903958e-1  5.903958e-1  4.0000e-1  5.1781e-1     1.4760\n    30  1.482481e-1  1.482481e-1  1.3333e-1  1.4642e-1     1.1119\n   100  4.122254e-2  4.122254e-2  4.0000e-2  4.1178e-2     1.0306\n  1000  4.011824e-3  4.011824e-3  4.0000e-3  4.0118e-3     1.0030"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "Paths for several impact parameters show the range from slight bending to a photon that circles the hole before escaping. The critical value is $b_c = 3\\sqrt{3}\\,M \\approx 5.196M$, the impact parameter of the photon sphere; a photon with $b < b_c$ falls in.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "photon_xy(bv) := block([phx, tr, ps, pr],\n  phx : deflect_numeric(bv) + float(%pi),\n  tr : np_cvode(photon_rhs, [ph, u, w], [0.0, 1.0/bv], np_linspace(0.0, phx, 800),\n                1e-11, 1e-13, adams),\n  ps : np_to_list(np_col(tr, 0)),\n  /* keep the part of the path within r = 40M */\n  pr : sublist(map(\"[\", ps, np_to_list(np_col(tr, 1))), lambda([pu], pu[2] > 1/40)),\n  [map(lambda([pu], cos(pu[1])/pu[2]), pr), map(lambda([pu], sin(pu[1])/pu[2]), pr)])$\nbs : [5.25, 6, 8, 12, 20]$\nbcols : [\"crimson\", \"darkorange\", \"seagreen\", \"steelblue\", \"purple\"]$\npaths : map(photon_xy, bs)$\napply(ax_draw2d, append(\n  apply(append, makelist([color = bcols[k], line_width = 2, name = sconcat(\"b = \", bs[k], \"M\"),\n                          lines(paths[k][1], paths[k][2])], k, 1, 5)),\n  [color = \"black\", name = \"Horizon r = 2M\", parametric(2*cos(v), 2*sin(v), v, 0, 2*%pi),\n   color = \"gray\", dash = \"dash\", name = \"Photon sphere r = 3M\",\n   parametric(3*cos(v), 3*sin(v), v, 0, 2*%pi),\n   aspect_ratio = true, xrange = [-25, 25], yrange = [-25, 25],\n   title = \"Light Paths Past a Black Hole\", xlabel = \"x / M\", ylabel = \"y / M\", showlegend = true]))$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 19,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "application/x-maxima-plotly": [
